CREATE INDEX idx_orders_cust_status_date ON orders (customer_id, status, order_date);
-- If your DB supports included columns (to make the index covering):
-- CREATE INDEX idx_orders_cust_status_date_inc ON orders (customer_id, status, order_date) INCLUDE (order_id, total_amount);

Explanation: The composite index (customer_id, status, order_date) matches the WHERE filters and the ORDER BY, allowing an index range scan and avoiding an expensive filesort; adding order_id and total_amount as included columns makes the index covering so the engine can satisfy the SELECT from the index alone.
